{% extends "base.html.j2" %}
{% block content %}
<section class="hero">
<span class="eyebrow">Weekly &middot; ranked &middot; calm</span>
<hgroup>
<h1>A quieter week, actually read.</h1>
<h2>Signalweek turns feeds, subscriptions, and inbox noise into one ranked digest every Monday.</h2>
</hgroup>
<p>
Stop skimming seven days of infinite scroll. Point Signalweek at the sources you
already follow and get a single, calmly organised read at the start of every week
&mdash; so you can catch what actually mattered and get on with the rest.
</p>
<div class="cta">
<a href="/signup" role="button">Create your account</a>
<a href="/login">or log in</a>
</div>
<div class="trust-bar" aria-label="What you get">
<span><svg viewBox="0 0 16 16" fill="currentColor" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M13.5 3.5 6 11 2.5 7.5l1-1L6 9l6.5-6.5z"/></svg> Ranks by signal, not recency</span>
<span><svg viewBox="0 0 16 16" fill="currentColor" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M13.5 3.5 6 11 2.5 7.5l1-1L6 9l6.5-6.5z"/></svg> RSS, Atom, and Hacker News</span>
<span><svg viewBox="0 0 16 16" fill="currentColor" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M13.5 3.5 6 11 2.5 7.5l1-1L6 9l6.5-6.5z"/></svg> Every archive exports as Markdown</span>
</div>
</section>

<section class="how-it-works" aria-labelledby="how-heading">
<h2 id="how-heading" class="section-heading">How it works</h2>
<ol class="steps">
<li>
<h3>Add your sources</h3>
<p>Paste feed URLs from the blogs, newsletters, and sites you already read. RSS or Atom, that's it.</p>
</li>
<li>
<h3>We collect the week</h3>
<p>Signalweek pulls new items across every source and groups them into a single ranked digest &mdash; deduped and quiet by design.</p>
</li>
<li>
<h3>Read one calm page</h3>
<p>Every Monday your digest is ready in the app and as Markdown. Skim it in five minutes; open only what earns the click.</p>
</li>
</ol>
</section>

<section class="sample-digest" aria-labelledby="sample-heading">
<p class="datestamp">Sample &middot; week of 2026-07-20</p>
<h3 id="sample-heading">This is roughly what a week looks like.</h3>
<section>
<h4>Julia Evans</h4>
<ul>
<li class="pinned">How I write a good git commit message
<small>A short, opinionated checklist &mdash; and why the subject line matters more than the body.</small>
</li>
<li>Debugging Kubernetes DNS at 2am
<small>The five things I check first when nothing resolves inside a pod.</small>
</li>
</ul>
</section>
<section>
<h4>Hacker News (top 3 of the week)</h4>
<ul>
<li>Show HN: I ran an SMTP server for a year</li>
<li class="pinned">The compiler will (not) save you</li>
<li>Postgres index-only scans in plain English</li>
</ul>
</section>
</section>

{% endblock %}
